<title>BELGIUM: Belgium to set up debt management agency.</title>
<headline>Belgium to set up debt management agency.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government has decided to set up an agency for the operational management of its state debt, the government said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The new agency will be part of the Treasury, it added.</p>
<p>At the end of February, Belgium had debts of 9,706 billion francs, at about 130 percent of GDP the highest in the European Union.</p>
<p>Further details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
